to-ubiquitination of TRAF6", "stId": "R-RNO-2730904", "stIdVersion": "R-RNO-2730904.1", "isInDisease": false, "isInferred": true, "maxDepth": 1, "name": ["Auto-ubiquitination of TRAF6"], "releaseDate": "2026-03-25", "speciesName": "Rattus norvegicus", "inferredFrom": [2730904], "species": [{"dbId": 48895, "displayName": "Rattus norvegicus", "name": ["Rattus norvegicus", "R. norvegicus", "Rn", "brown rat", "Norway rat"], "taxId": "10116", "abbreviation": "RNO", "className": "Species", "schemaClass": "Species"}], "category": "omitted", "className": "Reaction", "schemaClass": "BlackBoxEvent"}, {"dbId": 10046393, "displayName": "Auto-ubiquitination of TRAF6", "stId": "R-MMU-2730904", "stIdVersion": "R-MMU-2730904.1", "isInDisease": false, "isInferred": true, "maxDepth": 1, "name": ["Auto-ubiquitination of TRAF6"], "releaseDate": "2026-03-25", "speciesName": "Mus musculus", "inferredFrom": [2730904], "species": [{"dbId": 48892, "displayName": "Mus musculus", "name": ["Mus musculus", "M. musculus", "Mm", "house mouse"], "taxId": "10090", "abbreviation": "MMU", "className": "Species", "schemaClass": "Species"}], "category": "omitted", "className": "Reaction", "schemaClass": "BlackBoxEvent"}], "reviewed": [{"dbId": 3139040, "displayName": "Roncagalli, Romain, 2013-02-13", "dateTime": "2013-02-13 21:56:18", "className": "InstanceEdit", "schemaClass": "InstanceEdit"}], "species": [48887], "summation": [{"dbId": 202446, "displayName": "TRAF6 possesses ubiquitin ligase activity and undergoes K-63...", "text": "TRAF6 possesses ubiquitin ligase activity and undergoes K-63-linked auto-ubiquitination after its oligomerization. In the first step, ubiquitin is activated by an E1 ubiquitin activating enzyme. The activated ubiquitin is transferred to a E2 conjugating enzyme (a heterodimer of proteins Ubc13 and Uev1A) forming the E2-Ub thioester. Finally, in the presence of ubiquitin-protein ligase E3 (TRAF6, a RING-domain E3), ubiquitin is attached to the target protein (TRAF6 on residue Lysine 124) through an isopeptide bond between the C-terminus of ubiquitin and the epsilon-amino group of a lysine residue in the target protein. In contrast to K-48-linked ubiquitination that leads to the proteosomal degradation of the target protein, K-63-linked polyubiquitin chains act as a scaffold to assemble protein kinase complexes and mediate their activation through proteosome-independent mechanisms. This K63 polyubiquitinated TRAF6 activates the TAK1 kinase complex.", "literatureReference": [202511], "className": "Summation", "schemaClass": "Summation"}], "reviewStatus": {"dbId": 9821382, "displayName": "five stars", "definition": "externally reviewed", "name": ["five stars"], "className": "ReviewStatus", "schemaClass": "ReviewStatus"}, "category": "omitted", "catalystActivity": [{"dbId": 2730906, "displayName": "ubiquitin-protein transferase activity of DAG:p-5Y-PKC-theta:CBM oligomer:TRAF6 oligomer [plasma membrane]", "catalyzedEvent": [2730904], "physicalEntity": {"dbId": 2685713, "displayName": "DAG:p-5Y-PKC-theta:CBM oligomer:TRAF6 oligomer [plasma membrane]", "stId": "R-HSA-2685713", "stIdVersion": "R-HSA-2685713.1", "maxDepth": 4, "name": ["DAG:p-5Y-PKC-theta:CBM oligomer:TRAF6 oligomer"], "speciesName": "Homo sapiens", "catalystActivities": [2730906], "consumedByEvent": [2730904], "isChimeric": false, "species": [48887], "inDisease": false, "schemaClass": "Complex", "className": "Complex"}, "className": "CatalystActivity", "schemaClass": "CatalystActivity"}], "input": [{"dbId": 202463, "displayName": "UBE2N:UBE2V1 [cytosol]", "stId": "R-HSA-202463", "stIdVersion": "R-HSA-202463.2", "maxDepth": 2, "name": ["UBE2N:UBE2V1", "Ubc13:UBE2V1", "TRAF6-regulated IKK activator 1", "TRIKA1"], "speciesName": "Homo sapiens", "consumedByEvent": [2730904], "producedByEvent": [2730904], "species": [48887], "inDisease": false, "schemaClass": "Complex", "className": "Complex"}, {"dbId": 450152, "displayName": "K63polyUb [cytosol]", "stId": "R-HSA-450152", "stIdVe